-- GROUPS -- GENERATED by tools/classless-web/emit_group_data.py, do not hand-edit.
--
-- An ability is carried by a KIND of creature in a band of levels, not by one creature.
-- These two tables are that rule, in the smallest form the module can read it:
--
--   CLDB.groupmembers[g] = { rank spell ids }   the abilities of one group
--   CLDB.groupof[entry]  = { g, ... }           the groups one creature answers for
--
-- Together they answer "what can this creature drop" without a row per creature per
-- ability. The loot tables in classless_group_loot.sql are built from the same two.
if CLDB==nil then CLDB={} end
if CLDB.groupmembers==nil then CLDB.groupmembers={} end
if CLDB.groupof==nil then CLDB.groupof={} end

